WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:02.880
Is Holmes and Watson really that bad?

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:07.220
Apparently it is - since its Christmas Day
release, critics and audiences alike have

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:11.600
been teaming up to tear the project apart,
with even the rare good review still describing

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.100
considerable portions of the movie as "painful."

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.560
That's not how comedy is supposed to work.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.380
Here's why Holmes and Watson bombed.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:23.491
Whatever excitement there was for Holmes and
Watson was mostly due to the presence of its

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.380
two lead actors, John C. Reilly and Will Ferrell.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:31.580
The comedic duo first came together in a big
way for the 2006, country-fried comedy Talladega

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:35.870
Nights: The Ballad of Ricky Bobby, a sendup
of NASCAR and southern-style culture that

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:41.260
brought in over $162 million at the global
box office and gifted pop culture with quotes

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.920
that have withstood the test of time.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.240
“Shake and bake!”

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:45.960
“What does that do?

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:46.820
Does that blow your mind?

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:47.860
That.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:48.420
Just.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:48.920
Happened!”

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.200
That collaboration was followed in 2008 by
the even more enduringly-beloved Step Brothers,

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.720
which earned over $128 million globally.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.660
“Did we just become best friends?”

00:00:58.660 --> 00:00:59.160
“YUP!”

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:03.199
Though Reilly and Ferrell haven't gotten any
less funny over the years, their appeal as

00:01:03.199 --> 00:01:06.149
a comedic duo managed to fail them with Holmes
and Watson.

00:01:06.149 --> 00:01:11.390
A week after its release, the movie had only
earned around $24 million against an estimated

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:16.819
budget of at least $42 million - not exactly
the sign of a successful reunion.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:17.320
“Oh!

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:18.820
Amazing!”

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:23.700
Notoriously low review scores weren't the
only bad press Holmes and Watson received

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:24.789
during its rollout.

00:01:24.789 --> 00:01:29.079
The day after its theatrical release, Deadline
reported that the people responsible for Holmes

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:32.700
and Watson had actually tried to prevent the
movie from having a theatrical release at

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:33.200
all.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:37.600
Instead, executives tried to pass it off to
Netflix in an effort to contain the damage

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.300
- an offer which Netflix obviously refused.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.320
Reporter Anthony D'Alessandro wrote:

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.299
"[...] test scores for Holmes &amp; Watson were
so bad that Sony tried unloading the movie

00:01:46.299 --> 00:01:48.679
to Netflix, but the streamer wouldn't buy
it."

00:01:48.679 --> 00:01:52.909
It’s important to keep in mind that Netflix
is the streaming platform responsible for

00:01:52.909 --> 00:01:58.200
The Ridiculous 6 - a movie that has been consistent
in its zero percentage rating on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:03.400
It has been noted that the marketing campaign
for Holmes and Watson was curiously muted.

00:02:03.419 --> 00:02:08.119
In fact, if not for the wickedly poor reception
the movie received, it's possible you never

00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:09.129
would have heard of it.

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:13.319
When a studio is confident it has a hit on
its hands, like with Sony's own Spider-Man:

00:02:13.319 --> 00:02:17.780
Into the Spider-Verse, it tends to get the
word out early and promote the film as often

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:18.920
and widely as possible.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:23.819
In the case of Holmes and Watson, Sony seemingly
threw it into the crowded holiday mix, crossed

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.590
some fingers, and hoped no one would get too
mad.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.160
“Oooooh.”

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:30.379
“Are you quite sure this is a good idea?”

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:30.880
“This is fine!”

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:36.580
Holmes and Watson only managed to rake in
enough money to earn a number seven spot at

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:39.000
the domestic box office during its opening
weekend.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:43.870
This placed the brand new release behind second
weekend performances of Aquaman, Mary Poppins

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:48.480
Returns, and Bumblebee, as well as the third
weekend runs of Spider-Verse and The Mule.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:53.219
Holmes and Watson’s only saving grace would
be positive word-of-mouth, but even that seems

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:53.760
scarce.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:58.000
“Mr. Holmes, the empire is depending on
you.”

00:02:58.329 --> 00:03:02.100
Though fortunes have certainly turned for
movies with less-than-impressive debuts - such

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:06.780
as the remarkable run of 2017's The Greatest
Showman - Holmes and Watson seems to sorely

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:09.659
lack any crowd-pleasing qualities that could
redeem itself.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:15.580
In short, Holmes and Watson failed at the
box office because it was a failure of a film.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:20.100
Simply put, the so-called comedy couldn't
ignite the same passionate response as previous

00:03:20.109 --> 00:03:25.140
collaborations between its capable leads,
resulting in an inability to attract audiences

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.209
in the middle of a crowded holiday season.

00:03:27.209 --> 00:03:31.900
The broad critical consensus is that Holmes
and Watson is just not worth seeing, even

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.200
for curiosity's sake.

00:03:33.329 --> 00:03:37.700
At its best, Holmes and Watson is on the same
level of quality as some of those “cut for

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:41.620
time” Saturday Night Live sketches - the
kind that didn’t make it into the actual

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.440
live broadcast for good reason.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:47.940
The detective work here is simple elementary
- you’d be better off spending your money

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:48.959
on nachos.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:52.560
“They got bottomless nachos at Bennigan’s.”

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:55.620
“Gah, a whole mess of nachos sounds good
right now.”

